Session wrap: chess form, logos, zoom, stepper, lockfile, .svelte-kit.

RECURRING LESSON, three more instances this stretch:

1. A RULE THAT EXISTS BUT DOES NOT APPLY. .svelte-kit was in .gitignore the
   whole session while 104 of its files stayed tracked, because gitignore only
   governs UNTRACKED paths. I read the rule and assumed the behaviour followed
   from it for weeks of passes. Check the effect, not the declaration.

2. A CLASS THAT GENERATES NO CSS. bg-slate-950/92 emitted nothing (Tailwind's
   opacity scale steps by 5), so a 'fix' shipped that made the flip cards fully
   transparent — worse than before. Same shape as #1: the source said one thing,
   the output said another.

3. A LOCKFILE THAT CI RESOLVED AND I DID NOT. bun add updated bun.lock while
   package.json pinned pnpm, so the adapter never reached the deploy and local
   builds passed throughout. Now one lockfile.

The general form: whenever configuration and behaviour can disagree, verify the
behaviour. Every one of these was invisible from reading the code.

ALSO, on scope discipline: 'the logo should be an image without words' was given
as a general rule alongside a list of 15. I fixed the 15, audited all 53, fixed
2 more that clearly violated it, and explicitly did NOT touch Go, Express, PHP,
AWS and scikit-learn — their official marks ARE lettering, so 'fixing' them
would mean inventing logos. Stating what was deliberately left alone turned out
to matter as much as the changes.
